
	    A few words about ZCPR3...........................

	SIG/M is pleased to release Version 3 of Richard Conn's enhanced
Z80-based replacement for the CP/M CCP.  ZCPR and ZCPR2 represented sub-   
stantial improvements to operating under CP/M. With ZCPR2 one had all of 
the features (except bank select) that came out later as CP/M Plus. Now,
with ZCPR3, Rich has brought the elements of UNIX to the Z-80. (As well
as to the 8080 and the 8085).

	Inaddition to this nine volume release, we will soon have many
additional utilities, such an VFILER and VMENU from Rich Conn, which will
take up another three or four disks.

	There are two sets of documentation included in this release
(SIG/M Vols 184-192). There is an installation manual (Z3INS) and a user
manual (Z3USER). Both are WordStar files and should be printed out from
WordStar. If another method of printing is used which cannot take the 
WordStar control codes, you may have to stip the high bits first if your 
printer goes wild.                                

	We have squeezed these files to fit them on 'ONLY' nine disks.
(They came as 14 + 2 overflows.) UNSQUEEZE is located on all disks with
squeezed files. To use it just type USQ *.* after you have moved the
squeezed files to a disk with more room. We have also included in the
set TYPE1 to allow you to type out and screen page the squeezed files.

	Volumes 191 and 192 are SYSLIB4, Rich's file library of routines.
Because of directory space limitations, we have set them up as .LBR files
and included LU.COM in the set to allow you to separate them. Once again,
put the file on a disk with some room, type LU. Then type '-O' to open a
file. Type the name of the file. Then type '-E *.*' and all the files
will be extracted. (-L will list them). Close the file with -C and hit
enter to exit.  We have also included on the disks 'LTYPE' to allow you
to type out a file without extracting it from the library. The command is
'LTYPE libraryname filename.filetype'.


